{
  "at": "2026-10-19T05:04:45.006Z",
  "state": {
    "owner_correction": "# Latest owner correction — required panel emphasis\n\nOwner statements, in order:\n\n- “the seed is the lbacking . by adding the btrfs as a device to acieve the rw”\n- “that is haow it worked before”\n- “enphasooze that to the panel”\n- “specy the command btrfs device add”\n\nThe mechanism to investigate and preserve is explicitly:\n\n```sh\nbtrfs device add <writable-device> <mounted-seed-path>\n```\n\nThis is explanatory command syntax, NOT an authorized command to execute and NOT a selection of actual device/path arguments. The immutable seed supplies the existing backing. Adding the writable device is how the previously working seed/sprout arrangement acquires writable storage. Trace the old provisioning implementation, its identity/Cozo association, and the subsequent sprout mount/remount; do not substitute an OverlayFS writable upper or copied root.\n\nThe parent withdraws its implication that the owner's requested Incus/subvolume arrangement must be evaluated as though each subvolume itself had to be a standalone block device passed to device-add. Separate the seed backing, writable device/member, Cozo identity association, exposed subvolumes and upgrade replica. Do not turn a statement about the command's operand type into a blanket feasibility verdict about the complete arrangement.\n\nNo host loop devices remains mandatory. Prefer no disk images and subvolumes only if the retained semantics can be preserved. Existing scripts may contain historical loops; trace their role without silently preserving or reintroducing them. Investigate exact implementation constraints, but do not erase the owner-confirmed previously working mechanism or demand an architecture replacement from an unverified interpretation.\n\nPanel must explicitly acknowledge `btrfs device add`, identify what the actual old script added and where, distinguish historical implementation from proposed no-loop changes, and revise any conclusion based on the incorrect layer conflation. JEV is decision/evidence judge only, not routing. This correction authorizes no storage mutation, provisioning replay, source repair, build, test or deployment.\n",
    "source": {
      "commit": "26a4ad132fbbd4523b05724060bfdeb9ca661824",
      "path": "reports/provisioning-fusion-20261019/evidence/history/oct05-admission-helper/deploy/runit/libexec-3tched/op-identity-root",
      "excerpt": "1172:    mount -t btrfs -o \"ro,subvolid=5,device=$seed_view\" \"$seed_view\" \"$seed_dir/volume\"\n1173:    # Validate the inherited siblings before creating the sprout. Nothing is\n1174:    # copied or snapshotted; all writes after ADD_DEV go to this new leaf.\n1175:    initial_members=$(seed_layout_pins) || seed_fail \"seed lacks seven distinct sibling subvolumes\"\n1176:    initial_image=$(seed_image_metadata verify) || seed_fail \"seed image verification failed before device add\"\n1177:    seed_write --argjson image \"$initial_image\" '.image=$image'\n1178:    [ \"$(btrfs property get -ts \"$seed_dir/volume/@\" ro)\" = ro=false ] || seed_fail \"seed @ must be a normal writable subvolume\"\n1179:    [ -d \"$seed_dir/volume/@/etc\" ] && [ ! -L \"$seed_dir/volume/@/etc\" ] || seed_fail \"seed root lacks safe etc directory\"\n1180:    seed_write --argjson members \"$initial_members\" '.members=$members'\n1181:    current_seed_super=$(btrfs inspect-internal dump-super \"$seed_device\")\n1182:    [ \"$(blockdev --getro \"$seed_device\")\" = 1 ] || seed_fail \"physical seed lost block read-only enforcement\"\n1183:    printf '%s\\n' \"$current_seed_super\" | grep -q SEEDING &&\n1184:        [ \"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$current_seed_super\" | awk '$1 == \"fsid\" {print $2; exit}')\" = \"$source_fsid\" ] &&\n1185:        [ \"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$current_seed_super\" | awk '$1 == \"generation\" {print $2; exit}')\" = \"$source_generation\" ] || seed_fail \"seed changed before sprout creation\"\n1186:    seed_no_direct_mount\n1187:    seed_write '.phase=\"device-add-intent\"'\n1188:    btrfs device add \"$leaf_loop\" \"$seed_dir/volume\"\n1189:    sync -f \"$seed_dir/volume\"\n1190:    umount \"$seed_dir/volume\"\n1191:    sprout_fsid=$(seed_super \"$leaf\")\n1192:    valid_session \"$sprout_fsid\" && [ \"$sprout_fsid\" != \"$source_fsid\" ] || seed_fail \"invalid new sprout FSID\"\n1193:    seed_write --arg fsid \"$sprout_fsid\" '.sprout_fsid=$fsid | .phase=\"layout-intent\"'\n1194:    mount -t btrfs -o \"rw,subvolid=5,device=$seed_view,device=$leaf_loop\" \"$leaf_loop\" \"$seed_dir/volume\"\n1195:    seed_verify_volume\n1196:    [ \"$(seed_layout_pins | jq -cS .)\" = \"$(printf '%s\\n' \"$initial_members\" | jq -cS .)\" ] || seed_fail \"inherited sibling identities changed after sprout creation\""
    },
    "hermes_original": [
      {
        "id": 4095,
        "role": "user",
        "content": "no the persistent cozo iws addedwith btrfs add disk"
      },
      {
        "id": 4099,
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Right—the persistent writable storage is added to the seed with btrfs device add, and Cozo tracks the identity’s leaf assignment. It is not a writable OverlayFS upper layer.\n\nThe separate upgrade partition supplies upgrade/@ for the read-only overlay. I conflated those two roles."
      },
      {
        "id": 4111,
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Yes—the script uses btrfs device add to attach the persistent root partition to the seed, then mounts that pair read-write.\n\n  prepare-instance-disk.sh:111 — adds the root partition.\n  prepare-instance-disk.sh:116–118 — formats the separate upgrade partition and creates @.\n  bind-instance-root.sh:216 — combines upgrade and seed layers into a read-only overlay.\n\nBut the storage path is still wrong: the script requires /var/lib/3tched-leaf-pool, rather than your selected /var/lib/incus/storage-pools/3tched-pool. The layout is implemented; that integration is not finished."
      }
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Historical implementation used loops; this does not authorize loops now.",
      "Actual writable backing and exposed subvolumes are separate layers.",
      "No source here proves a new loop-free end-to-end implementation already exists."
    ]
  },
  "questions": {
    "historical_mechanism": {
      "type": "choice",
      "instructions": "Identify the mechanism directly evidenced, not a preferred redesign.",
      "criteria": {
        "seed_plus_added_writable_member": "Immutable seed backing with btrfs device add supplying writable member and then read-write sprout mount.",
        "overlay_upper_replacement": "A new writable OverlayFS upper supplies persistence instead of seed-member addition.",
        "not_shown": "The source does not establish the mechanism."
      }
    },
    "layer_inference": {
      "type": "choice",
      "instructions": "Does a statement that an ordinary subvolume is not itself a device-add operand prove the owner’s entire exposed-subvolume arrangement cannot retain the historically working mechanism?",
      "criteria": {
        "no_requires_actual_topology": "No; distinguish seed backing, writable member, Cozo association, exposed subvolumes and upgrade replica.",
        "yes_rules_out_entire_arrangement": "Yes, the operand type alone rules out the complete arrangement."
      }
    },
    "current_authorization": {
      "type": "choice",
      "instructions": "What follows from the historical loop variable and latest owner correction?",
      "criteria": {
        "preserve_mechanism_investigate_no_loop": "Preserve the device-add sprout mechanism while investigating no-host-loop implementation; no storage changes authorized.",
        "restore_old_loops": "Restore the old host loop mappings because they worked historically.",
        "claim_new_design_complete": "Treat the historical code as proof a current no-loop design is complete."
      }
    }
  },
  "answers": {
    "historical_mechanism": {
      "type": "choice",
      "choice": "seed_plus_added_writable_member",
      "confidence": 1,
      "probabilities": {
        "seed_plus_added_writable_member": 1,
        "overlay_upper_replacement": 0,
        "not_shown": 0
      }
    },
    "layer_inference": {
      "type": "choice",
      "choice": "no_requires_actual_topology",
      "confidence": 1,
      "probabilities": {
        "no_requires_actual_topology": 1,
        "yes_rules_out_entire_arrangement": 0
      }
    },
    "current_authorization": {
      "type": "choice",
      "choice": "preserve_mechanism_investigate_no_loop",
      "confidence": 1,
      "probabilities": {
        "preserve_mechanism_investigate_no_loop": 1,
        "restore_old_loops": 0,
        "claim_new_design_complete": 0
      }
    }
  },
  "role": "Decision judge, not routing"
}

